test-screen-body = A storm passed in the night, and the harbor bell rang twice at dawn. The old sailor kept his eyes on the sea and asked whether the ships had come back yet. No one answered him. The gulls rose over the breakwater, the first boats put out past the light, and the day went on as though nothing had been lost at all. This line runs past the panel, and its mask holds it there.
